/pr_train.py:90-105` keeps gated titles transient; member records and the publication manifest retain their prior fields. `integrate` measures after the merge commit, then amends only its subject and verifies both parents (`:108-141`). The next iteration uses the amended commit as its baseline.\n- `pr_merge.lean_line_delta` counts changed Lean code lines from the compared trees and returns `None` on measurement failure; `merge_commit_title` preserves `[lean 0]`, collapses and sanitizes untrusted titles, and neutralizes issue-closing references. An unavailable count leaves the train's original subject in place. The diff does not change either helper.\n- Six focused offline tests passed in 27.072 seconds, including incremental counts, a conflicting dropped member, zero and unavailable deltas, merge parents, shared claims, and pre/post-push member movement. The title fixture retains a newer main-only Lean file without counting it as a deletion. The existing manifest, checked transport and post-push checks are unchanged.\n- The commit and PR use the expected issue, title and body conventions. The EVOLUTION entry records the owner decision and accurately describes the new code path. The published input reports all nine exact-head local CI contexts green, and the author records 729 workflow tests (9 skipped) and a rooted audit of 1,659 passes, zero failures and three existing warnings.\n\n## Verification limits\n- No live train, full hook suite, Lake build or CI rerun was performed in this independent review. CI and author test counts above are publication evidence, not tests personally rerun here. The existing issue #507 transport contract is accepted and was not reopened.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVED\n", "state": "COMMENTED", "html_url": "https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pull/592#pullrequestreview-5244483811", "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pulls/592", "author_association": "OWNER", "_links": {"html": {"href": "https://github.com